  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a **palindromic** string `s`.\n\nOutput the **lexicographically smallest** palindromic permutation of `s`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"z\"\n\n**Output:** \"z\"\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nA string of only one character is already the lexicographically smallest palindrome.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"babab\"\n\n**Output:** \"abbba\"\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nRearranging `\"babab\"` → `\"abbba\"` gives the smallest lexicographic palindrome.\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"daccad\"\n\n**Output:** \"acddca\"\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nRearranging `\"daccad\"` → `\"acddca\"` gives the smallest lexicographic palindrome.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 105`\n* `s` is composed of lowercase English letters.\n* `s` is guaranteed to be palindromic.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
